From 2c68f9c0fdc11e85695b07a98f2ba68845976007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:10:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/52] ppc-darwin: d8 --apply-priority without the 10.10
 thread-QoS API

G5 parade #9 of the 12.4 port (d8.cc, the first d8 TU - the d8
target's objects compile only after its library dependencies are
complete, so mksnapshot ran to completion with patch 0048):

  d8.cc:5763: error: 'QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE' was not declared
  d8.cc:5763: error: 'pthread_set_qos_class_self_np' was not declared

PowerPC-era-SDK class (0038, 0044, 0047).  Shell::Main's
--apply-priority block under V8_OS_DARWIN sets the mach task-category
policy (10.4-era API, compiled fine) and then the thread QoS class,
which only exists from the 10.10 SDK on.  Gate the QoS call on the
deployment target like semaphore.cc (0019) and platform-darwin.cc
(0047): MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= 101000, with the
<AvailabilityMacros.h> include added to the existing V8_OS_DARWIN
include block; >= 10.10 builds compile upstream's line unchanged, the
PowerPC targets keep the task-policy half of the option.

d8 sweep: the six d8 TUs the harness builds (d8, d8-console, d8-js,
d8-test, d8-platforms, d8-posix, async-hooks-wrapper) have no other
Darwin-only API and no post-10.5 libc call (std::getline is the C++
library); d8-posix.cc's WNOWAIT block already excludes __APPLE__.

Note for a later full rebuild, not changed here to keep this cycle to
one TU: 0038 gated platform-posix.cc's QoS switch on
defined(QOS_CLASS_BACKGROUND), but sys/qos.h declares the QOS_CLASS_*
values as enum members, not macros, so that test is false on every
SDK - identical binaries on PowerPC (compiled out either way), but a
>= 10.10 build of the patched tree loses thread QoS.  Unify it on the
deployment-target test used here when platform-posix.cc next
recompiles anyway.
---
 v8/src/d8/d8.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/d8/d8.cc b/v8/src/d8/d8.cc
index 7740363..0f18b42 100644
--- a/v8/src/d8/d8.cc
+++ b/v8/src/d8/d8.cc
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
 #include "src/utils/utils.h"
 
 #ifdef V8_OS_DARWIN
+#include <AvailabilityMacros.h>
 #include <mach/mach.h>
 #include <mach/task_policy.h>
 #endif
@@ -5760,7 +5761,12 @@ int Shell::Main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
                                                 TASK_FOREGROUND_APPLICATION};
     task_policy_set(mach_task_self(), TASK_CATEGORY_POLICY,
                     (task_policy_t)&category, TASK_CATEGORY_POLICY_COUNT);
+    // The thread QoS API appeared in 10.10; on the PowerPC-era SDKs the
+    // task-category policy above is the whole of --apply-priority.
+#if !defined(MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED) || \
+    MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= 101000
     pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE, 0);
+#endif
   }
 #endif
 
